{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.JetSwTauDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.JetSwTauDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.jet_sw_tau_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.jet_sw_tau_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L73-L82","doc":"**L2.** The τ-image of the MI integral is the sum over jet degrees of\nthe prolonged Seiberg–Witten periods.  **Derived** (not projected):\nrewrite `τ` to the graded sum (`tau_additive`), then rewrite each\nsummand `tauGraded n` to the SW period `period n`\n(`graded_eq_period`).  Neither hypothesis field is this conclusion. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:jet-sw-tau-decomposition","label":"prop:jet-sw-tau-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.graded_eq_period","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.graded_eq_period","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L71-L71","doc":"**`prop:mi-sw-abelianisation`**: each jet graded piece's τ-image is\nthe `n`-th prolonged SW period.  A structural *hypothesis*, not the\ngraded-sum conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.tau_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.tau_additive","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L67-L67","doc":"**Additivity / exhaustiveness of `τ`** (the \"observe last\"\nprinciple): `τ` collapses the jet tower to the graded sum of the\nτ-images of its graded pieces.  A structural *hypothesis* — its\nright-hand side sums `tauGraded`, not `period`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.tauValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.tauValue","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The Archimedean value `τ(MI∫_{S_c})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.tauGraded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.tauGraded","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The τ-image `τ(graded_n)` of the `n`-th vertical (jet) graded piece\nof the MI integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.period","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.period","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The `n`-th prolonged SW period `a_D^{(n)} = ∮ λ_SW^{(n)}`\n(`prop:sw-period-residue-sum`: an algebraic residue sum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.maxOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.maxOrder","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Highest vertical (jet) degree retained. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.JetSWArchDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/jet-sw-tau-decomposition.lean#L46-L71","doc":"**Jet / τ decomposition data**.  All fields are *inputs*: the\nprolonged SW periods, the τ-value of the MI integral, the τ-image of\neach jet graded piece, and the two structural hypotheses (additivity\nof `τ` on the associated graded, and the identification of each\ngraded piece with a SW period).  None is the conclusion\n`tauValue = ∑ period n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}